# LANDING-LOCK template (design 5.9)
#
# The live file is normally ABSENT or EMPTY — that is what "free" means
# (design: "absent/empty = free"). It exists with exactly one line only
# while a landing is in progress, created atomically so the first
# announcer wins (design: "Created atomically (one writer wins); released
# right after the push"). Release means deleting the file (or truncating it
# to empty) immediately after the push completes.
#
# Format (this exact shape is what scripts/hooks/pre-push-ledger-check
# parses — a format change here must land together with a matching change
# to that script):
#
#   squad=<squad-id> branch=<branch-name> taken-at=<ISO8601>
#
# Example (illustration only — do not leave this file present with content
# when nothing is actually landing):
# squad=squad-security branch=release/v0.1.1 taken-at=2026-09-25T09:15:00Z
